{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/483948-new-gmc-devotions","id":483948,"title":"New GMC Devotions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-17T15:33:40-07:00","id":483948,"title":"New GMC Devotions","content":"Constructive feedback is very welcome.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"color:#cc0000\">Abominable Weaponry (Vigor 5, Protean 4)</span></span></b><br /> <br /> The Kindred who possess this Devotion are not to be trifled with. They can manifest truly horrible natural weapons.<br /> <br /> Cost: 10 Vitae<br /> Dice Pool: None<br /> Action: Reflexive<br /> <br /> The Kindred grows thrashing, barbed tendrils from all over his body, changes his hands into humongous claws or his arm into a steel piercing sword and so on. He may make Brawl or Weaponry attacks that have a +2A damage bonus and Armor Piercing 4 for the rest of the scene. Resilience offers no protection against this Devotion, but a related Devotion does (see below). This Devotion costs 5 Experiences.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#cc0000\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Abominable Armor (Resilience 5, Protean 4)</span></span></b><br /> <br /> The Kindred who possess this Devotion are hard to take down. They can manifest very persistent natural armor.<br /> <br /> Cost: 10 Vitae<br /> Dice Pool: None<br /> Action: Reflexive<br /> <br /> The Kindred applies his Resilience as Armor against all attacks (including the previous Devotion) for the remainder of the scene, but he is covered in some obvious protection: chitin or bone plates, jagged obsidian or crystallized blood. Sunlight still causes damage. This Devotion costs 5 Experiences.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"color:#cc0000\">One Drop, Great Mending (Vigor 3, Resilience 3, Celerity 3)</span></span></b><br /> <br /> The Kindred\u2019s Vitae is more efficient at regenerating his undead body than usual.<br /> <br /> Cost: None<br /> Dice Pool: None<br /> Action: None (always active)<br /> <br /> Every point of Vitae heals 2 lethal or 3 bashing. Healing 1 aggravated only costs 3 Vitae. This Devotion costs 3 Experiences. There is an advanced version which requires Vigor 4, Resilience 4, Celerity 4 and Blood Potency 6. This version makes each Vitae heal 3 lethal, and allows you to heal 1 aggravated with 3 Vitae and no sleeping. The advanced version costs 6 Experiences.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"color:#cc0000\">Relentless Mauling (Vigor 3, Resilience 3, Celerity 3)</span></span></b><br /> <br /> The Kindred can strike multiple foes in one turn.<br /> <br /> Cost: 3 Vitae or 5 Vitae (Advanced)<br /> Dice Pool: None<br /> Action: Reflexive<br /> <br /> Upon a successful Brawl or Weaponry attack, double the amount of total points of damage dealt and divide them between two or more targets. Each target may only receive as much damage as your base successes. Example: your vampire grows natural weapons by using Predatory Aspect, Unnatural Aspect, Abominable Aspect or some other power. Let\u2019s say you get 3 successes and your weapon has a damage bonus of 2. [3 + 2] x 2 = 10 points of damage to be distributed, but each target may only receive up to 3 points of damage. This Devotion costs 3 Experiences. The advanced version requires Vigor 5, Resilience 5 and Celerity 5, which quadruples your total success before division. The advanced version costs 6 Experiences.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"color:#cc0000\">Face Of Myth And Legend (Vigor 5, Resilience 5, Protean 4)</span></span></b><br /> <br /> The Kindred can take on the shape of a mythological creature. He does not have to mimic the exact description of said creature, and may even customize the appearance of this new form.<br /> <br /> Cost: 9 Vitae + 1 willpower<br /> Dice Pool: None<br /> Action: Reflexive<br /> <br /> At the moment of activation, choose a type of monster. Each type favors two Attributes of one category. Mental = Intelligence and Wits, Physical = Strength and Stamina, and Social = Presence and Manipulation. While in this form, both of the favored Attributes receive dots equal to the Kindred\u2019s Blood Potency, which also increases derived stats. The favored Attributes may be taken beyond 10 dots. You may partially channel the powers of the Devotion. This allows you to keep your normal form, but each favored Attribute only gains Blood Potency/2 round up in dots, or one favored Attribute gains full Blood Potency in dots. While suppressing the Devotion, some feature associated with it must poke through the disguise for the benefits to be received. This may include body modifications, behavior tics and transformations in the surroundings. The flaws in the disguise stack with any telling signs of the Clan. The effect lasts for the remainder of the scene, during which you may reflexively change between partial and complete forms by spending 1 Vitae. This Devotion costs 5 Experiences.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"color:#cc0000\">Barbed Lashing (Majesty 3 or Dominate 3 or Nightmare 3)</span></span></b><br /> <br /> The Kindred with this Devotion can hone his specialization in Lashing Out into a more potent form.<br /> <br /> Cost: 1 Vitae<br /> Dice Pool: None<br /> Action: Reflexive<br /> <br /> The Kindred must have one of the Lashing Out Merits: Cutthroat, Enticing or Atrocious. These are improved with Dominate 3, Majesty 3 or Nightmare 3, respectively. The 8 Again bonus becomes the Rote Quality. This Devotion costs 3 Experiences.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"color:#cc0000\">The Beast Made Flesh (Protean 5, Vigor 5, Blood Potency 6)</span></span></b><br /> <br /> The Kindred can sacrifice a great deal of his Vitae to summon a bloody conduit for the Beast that is every bit as physical as it is the stuff of nightmares.<br /> <br /> Cost: 15 Vitae + 1 willpower DOT<br /> Dice Pool: None<br /> Action: Instant<br /> <br /> The Kindred releases a pitch black substance that is mist, blood, undead body parts and hellish visions all at the same time. The Beast enters this substance and shapes it into an avatar for itself that is mostly obedient. The avatar remains active indefinitely, unless it is destroyed. This Devotion costs 6 Experiences.<br /> <br /> Treat the Beast Made Flesh as a pseudo ephemeral being with the following stats. There are legends among the Kindred of Elders of very high Blood Potency and occult knowledge who can create avatars for the Beast with Rank 6 or more, truly god-like monstrosities of the night. Some even say that this is how a Clan Progenitor or some Demons of the Inferno come to be.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank:</b> 5<br /> <br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Power 15, Finesse 15, Resistance 15<br /> <br /> <b>Size: </b>10<br /> <br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 25<br /> <br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <br /> <b>Defense:</b> 10<br /> <br /> <b>Initiative Mod:</b> 15<br /> <br /> <b>Speed:</b> 20<br /> <br /> <b>Max Vitae/Per Turn:</b> 50/15<br /> <br /> <b>Influence:</b> Fear 5, Desire 5<br /> <br /> <b>Manifestation:</b> Twilight Form, Materialize, Image, Fetter, Unfetter, Possess<br /> <br /> <b>Ban:</b> the Beast Made Flesh always follows orders with the monstrous twists inherent to its nature. If asked to kill, it leaves behind utterly mangled corpses and trails of viscera. If asked to seduce, it appeals to the darkest urges of the soul. If asked to frighten, victims are turned into catatonic shells. It is incapable of compassion or self denial, and will not spare the Kindred\u2019s allies and loved ones if provoked into frenzy. It is only a step from there for the Kindred to lose control of it.<br /> <br /> <b>Bane:</b> sunlight. Fire only deals lethal damage.<br /> <br /> <b>Numina:</b> Mortal Mask, Awe, Terrify, Speed, Morphic Form, Powered By Blood<br /> <br /> <b>Powered By Blood:</b> The Beast Made Flesh uses Vitae instead of Essence. It restores Vitae very violently: it deals supernatural lethal damage with Armor Piercing and damage bonus equal to Rank and steals 1 Vitae for every point of damage dealt, with no grapple required. It may use Vitae to heal itself like Kindred and improve any Attribute like ephemeral beings.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"color:#cc0000\">Rip The Vital Ichor (Blood Potency 6, Protean 4, Vigor 3) + Optional Claws Of The Unholy</span></span></b><br /> <br /> Cost: 1 willpower point per attack<br /> Dice Pool: None<br /> Action: Reflexive<br /> <br /> You have modified your Horrid Talons granted by Protean 4 to be capable of dealing damage and absorbing Vitae in one go, without a grapple. Each point of lethal damage dealt gives you 1 Vitae. If you have Claws Of The Unholy, each aggravated damage dealt gives you 3 Vitae. This Devotion costs 4 Experiences.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"color:#cc0000\">Beast\u2019s Bones (Blood Potency 6, Protean 3, Celerity 3, Resilience 3)</span></span></b><br /> <br /> Cost: None<br /> Dice Pool: None<br /> Action: Reflexive<br /> <br /> You do not need to consume the blood of the animals you wish to transform into. You still have a maximum number of forms ready equal to your Protean dots, but they can be anything within the parameters set by &quot;Beast's Skin&quot;. Changing your stored forms still requires a a day and a night of sleep on your Unmarked Grave, however. This Devotion costs 4 Experiences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-27-2015, 04:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-18T15:02:40-07:00","id":484860,"title":"","content":"Only note on the beast made flesh, wouldn't it be terrible (read: interesting) if it had a chance to give birth to a strix. <br /> <br /> To me the balance seems off generally but I have yet to play a high end vampire game so me eye balling it isn't exactry the most accurate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-18T21:32:13-07:00","id":485063,"title":"","content":"I'd turn abominable aspect into 2 different devotions- one to enhance their offensive power using protean and vigor, another protecting their bodies with resilience and protean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-18T21:52:27-07:00","id":485076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/483948-new-gmc-devotions?p=484860#post484860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only note on the beast made flesh, wouldn't it be terrible (read: interesting) if it had a chance to give birth to a strix.<br /> <br /> To me the balance seems off generally but I have yet to play a high end vampire game so me eye balling it isn't exactry the most accurate.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be terrible and interesting indeed!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/483948-new-gmc-devotions?p=485063#post485063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'd turn abominable aspect into 2 different devotions- one to enhance their offensive power using protean and vigor, another protecting their bodies with resilience and protean.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, that does sound more balanced. I edited accordingly.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"